{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CggAU6iq3WxU8h8iqR2uU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I don't have any database-query or network tools in this session — no gnomAD, Ensembl, or dbSNP access, and no shell. So the following is **from my own knowledge**, not a live lookup, and I'm flagging the precision limits accordingly.\n\n## Gene and variant identity (high confidence)\n\n**rs1801133 is in *MTHFR*** (methylenetetrahydrofolate reductase), chromosome 1p36.22.\n\n- Known clinically as the **MTHFR C677T** variant\n- Coding change: `NM_005957.4:c.665C>T`, p.(Ala222Val) — the \"677\" and \"A222V\" labels come from an older transcript numbering that is still in universal clinical use\n- Position: chr1:11,796,321 (GRCh38) / chr1:11,856,378 (GRCh37)\n- Risk/minor allele: **T**\n\n## Allele frequency (approximate — recalled, not retrieved)\n\nThe T allele is common and strongly population-stratified. Approximate frequencies:\n\n| Population | T allele freq (approx.) |\n|---|---|\n| Global | ~0.25–0.33 |\n| Non-Finnish European | ~0.33 |\n| Admixed American / Latino | ~0.45–0.48 |\n| East Asian | ~0.30–0.40 |\n| Finnish | ~0.25–0.30 |\n| Ashkenazi Jewish | ~0.30–0.35 |\n| South Asian | ~0.12–0.15 |\n| African / African-American | ~0.10–0.12 |\n\nTwo caveats worth stating plainly:\n\n1. **I cannot give you the exact gnomAD figure.** The global AF differs noticeably between gnomAD versions (v2 exomes vs. v4, which is far more European-weighted), so quoting a single number to three decimal places from memory would be guesswork. For the citable value, query gnomAD directly at `https://gnomad.broadinstitute.org/variant/1-11796321-C-T?dataset=gnomad_r4` (GRCh38 coordinates above).\n2. Because the T allele exceeds 5% in every major population, it fails any rarity filter for pathogenicity — consistent with its ClinVar classification as a risk/benign-spectrum variant rather than a Mendelian disease allele. Homozygous TT runs roughly 10–12% in Europeans.\n\n## ANSWER\n\n**Gene: *MTHFR*** (methylenetetrahydrofolate reductase), chr1p36.22; the variant is the well-known **C677T**, `NM_005957.4:c.665C>T`, p.Ala222Val, at chr1:11,796,321 C>T (GRCh38).\n\n**Allele frequency: I could not retrieve the exact gnomAD value — no database tool available in this session.** From recall, the T allele is ~0.25–0.33 globally, ~0.33 in non-Finnish Europeans, ~0.45–0.48 in Latino/Admixed American, ~0.30–0.40 East Asian, ~0.10–0.12 African. Verify at gnomAD v4, variant `1-11796321-C-T`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":18917,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":18917},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e87b829f-0362-413e-9374-6c88bccc1af7","uuid":"00377537-670d-46d7-9c6d-5cbb2858fa12","timestamp":"2026-11-03T14:37:42.134Z","request_id":"req_011CggAU6MGNqLTfH9NN4bUg"}
